RepDay — Complete Functional & UI Specification (Android Rebuild Blueprint)
1. Product Overview & Architecture
RepDay is an offline, local-first Material 3 strength-training and workout-logging application built for fast, one-handed gym-floor logging.
Core Principles
Local-First & Zero Auth: All routines, training plans, active sessions, completed history, preferences, and the custom exercise library are stored strictly on-device (Android equivalent: Room SQLite for structured entities + Jetpack DataStore for settings/theme/active-session snapshot). No backend or account login is required.
One-Handed Gym Ergonomics: Minimum 44dp–48dp touch targets across all interactive controls, monospace tabular numerals (fontFeatureSettings = "tnum") for all weights/reps/timers, collapsed-by-default exercise cards during live workouts with automatic advance, and single-tap previous-set auto-fill.
Zero AI / Gemini Dependency: See Section 8 — despite @google/genai existing in the template package.json, the application makes zero Gemini API calls and contains zero LLM prompts. Every feature (autocomplete, exercise swap scoring, plate math, plan progression, theme contrast calculation) is 100% deterministic and offline.
