2.4 Dynamic Token Derivation Algorithm
From the 4 active base colors (canvas, surface, accent, text), compute isDarkCanvas = relativeLuminance(canvas) < 0.25 (WCAG 2.1 sRGB luminance), then derive all semantic tokens via linear RGB interpolation mix(a, b, weightB):
surfaceAlt: Dark mix(canvas, surface, 0.55) | Light mix(surface, canvas, 0.65)
surfaceElevated: Dark mix(surface, #FFFFFF, 0.07) | Light mix(surface, #000000, 0.05)
border: mix(surface, text, 0.14)
borderStrong: mix(surface, text, 0.24)
textSecondary: Dark mix(text, surface, 0.26) | Light mix(text, surface, 0.32)
textMuted: Dark mix(text, surface, 0.44) | Light mix(text, surface, 0.48)
accentFg: Whichever of #0E1013 or #FFFFFF has the higher WCAG contrast ratio against accent
accentHover: Dark mix(accent, #FFFFFF, 0.14) | Light mix(accent, #000000, 0.12)
accentSoft: Dark mix(surface, accent, 0.18) | Light mix(surface, accent, 0.14)
accentSoftFg: Dark mix(accent, #FFFFFF, 0.22) | Light mix(accent, #000000, 0.28)
Success (ok): Dark (ok=#7CE8A5, okSurface=mix(surface,#1E824C,0.22), okInput=mix(surface,#1E824C,0.34), okFg=#E7FBEF); Light (ok=#157A44, okSurface=mix(surface,#157A44,0.11), okInput=mix(surface,#157A44,0.18), okFg=#0E4E2B)
Danger: Dark (danger=#FF8A80, dangerSurface=mix(surface,#D32F2F,0.24)); Light (danger=#C62828, dangerSurface=mix(surface,#C62828,0.10))
