6. Critical Business Rules & Edge Cases
Drop Set Zero-Rest Rule (enforceDropSetRestRules):
Whenever set i + 1 has tag == DROP, set i is automatically forced to restSeconds = 0 ("No rest") across the Routine Editor, Routine preview, and Active Workout.
If set i + 1 is untagged from DROP or deleted while set i had restSeconds == 0 (and the new set i + 1 isn't also DROP), restore set i to the exercise's default rest.
Duplicating a set whose rest was zeroed only because a drop set followed it restores the exercise's default rest on the cloned set unless the clone itself precedes a drop set.
Non-Reversed Targets & Derived Summaries:
Rep ranges (1–100) and RPE targets (6.0–10.0, snapped to 0.5) can never be reversed (7-5 normalizes to 5-7; 8-8 collapses to 8).
Every planned set must have at least one target (repRange, targetRpe, or both).
Exercise-level summary repRange and targetRpe are dynamically derived as the min–max envelope across all planned sets (e.g., sets of 8, 5, 4-6, 8-10 summarize as 4-10; RPE-only sets produce empty repRange = "" and format as 3 × RPE 8).
Drift-Free Rest Timer: Store an absolute target timestamp endTime = now + durationMs and compute remainingSeconds = ceil((endTime - now) / 1000) on a 250ms tick (or Android ForegroundService / AlarmManager notification so the timer survives backgrounding and screen lock).
Greedy Plate Calculator Math: Perform subtraction in integer hundredths (round(value * 100)) descending through sorted enabled plates to prevent floating-point drift on 2.5 and 1.25 plates.
Plan Progress & Weekly Compliance:
elapsedWeeks = floor((now - startedAt) / 7_DAYS_MS), currentWeek = clamp(elapsedWeeks + 1, 1, totalWeeks).
Current week window is [startedAt + (currentWeek - 1) * 7d, +7d).
Each slot's weekly completion count is capped at slot.timesPerWeek when summing the block's weekly progress total so doing one routine 3 times doesn't mask a missed second routine.
Routine History Matching (matchesRoutineHistory): Matches if workout.routineId == routine.id, OR (fallback for legacy/renamed/deleted logs) case-insensitive normalized routine names match.
Duplicate Naming Collision Prevention: Strips existing (Copy) / (Copy N) suffix, then appends (Copy), (Copy 2), (Copy 3), etc., until unique case-insensitively.
Accidental Modal Dismiss Protection: Only dismiss modal sheets/dialogs on scrim tap when touch-down AND touch-up occur outside the sheet (native Compose ModalBottomSheet handles this automatically, avoiding web text-drag dismissal bugs).
7. Key End-to-End User Flows
Create & Run a Custom Routine: Routines tab → New Routine → enter name + exercises (picking from autocomplete or typing a brand-new movement, which auto-saves to library) → optionally expand sets to add Warm-up / Top / Backoff / Drop Set tags, Target RPE, and per-set rest → Create Routine → tap Start → tap first exercise to expand → tap Prev or enter Weight/Reps → tap Done checkbox → rest timer auto-starts → finishing last set auto-collapses exercise and opens the next → tap Finish → add notes → Save Workout → redirects to History.
Mid-Workout Adaptation: Inside Active Workout → machine is taken → tap Reorder to drag/move exercise lower, OR tap Swap on the exercise to pick a keyword-matched alternative (or type a custom one, auto-saved to library), OR tap Plates to compute exact barbell/machine plate loading.
Multi-Block Plan with Future Placeholders: Plans tab → New Plan → select Training Blocks → Block 1 (4w) add existing routines at 1×/wk → + Add Block → Block 2 (4w) add placeholder workouts (Upper Hypertrophy, Lower Hypertrophy) → Create Plan → Set Active → later expand plan card and tap Build Routine on Upper Hypertrophy → Routine Editor opens prefilled → saving automatically creates the routine and links it into Block 2.
Per-Routine Progress Review: On any Routine card, tap Last done 2 days ago (3) (or ⋮ -> History) → switches to History tab pre-filtered to that routine, updating the Workouts/Volume/Duration summary strip and auto-expanding the latest log.
8. Gemini Prompts & AI Features
Current App Status: None. RepDay contains zero Gemini API integrations, zero system instructions, and zero prompt templates. All logic (including exercise swap suggestions, custom exercise library management, plate breakdown, and contrast calculations) runs deterministically and offline on-device.
For Your Native Android Rebuild: Do not include the Gemini SDK, API key configuration, or network permissions unless you intentionally decide to add new AI features later. Keeping the app 100% offline guarantees instant gym-floor responsiveness in low-signal basements/gyms.
